--TEST--
A property declaring a `get` hook and no `set` hook is not written, while a `set` hook and the hook's own backing slot still are (`rule:classes/property-hooks`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Reading {
    public int $raw;

    // Both hooks: the write runs `set`, which commits through the backing
    // slot — the one place `$this->doubled` is the slot and not a call.
    public int $doubled {
        get => $this->raw * 2;
        set(int $v) { $this->raw = $v - 2; }
    }

    // `get` alone. The accessor is the whole of what this property answers
    // with, so a write has nothing to commit through: Novis refuses it
    // rather than storing into a slot the `get` hook may never read.
    public int $tripled {
        get => $this->raw * 3;
    }

    public function constructor(int $raw) {
        $this->raw = $raw;
    }

    // Legal: inside the declaring class, `$this->tripled` is the backing
    // slot every hooked property keeps, which is how a `get`-only property
    // is given a value at all.
    public function arm(int $v): void {
        $this->tripled = $v;
    }
}

Reading $r = new Reading(4);

// Legal: `raw` is plain storage and `doubled` has a `set` hook.
$r->raw = 10;
$r->doubled = 8;
echo $r->doubled, ";", $r->tripled, "\n";

// Refused, at every spelling that writes.
$r->tripled = 9;
$r->tripled += 1;
$r->tripled++;
// covers: lang:classes/property-hooks
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0787]: `Reading::$tripled` declares a `get` hook and no `set` hook, so only `Reading` writes it
%A
error[E0787]: `Reading::$tripled` declares a `get` hook and no `set` hook, so only `Reading` writes it
%A
error[E0787]: `Reading::$tripled` declares a `get` hook and no `set` hook, so only `Reading` writes it
%A
